 "functions": [],
 "react": [
  {
   "component": "BudgetGuard",
   "exported": true,
   "props": [
    {
     "name": "limits",
     "type": "BudgetLimit[]",
     "optional": true,
     "description": "The limits – the first one is the big meter. Controlled when defined (a live run passes its numbers in): pair\nwith onLimitsChange or onRaise and pass the raised cap back. Otherwise the component keeps them, starting from\n`defaultLimits`"
    },
    {
     "name": "defaultLimits",
     "type": "BudgetLimit[]",
     "optional": true,
     "description": "Initial limits when uncontrolled"
    },
    {
     "name": "onLimitsChange",
     "type": "(limits: BudgetLimit[]) => void",
     "optional": true,
     "description": "Every raise, with all the limits after it"
    },
    {
     "name": "onRaise",
     "type": "(id: string, cap: number, previous: number) => void",
     "optional": true,
     "description": "A cap raised from the warning or the stop: the limit's id, its new cap and the one before"
    },
    {
     "name": "onCapReach",
     "type": "(id: string, limit: BudgetLimit) => void",
     "optional": true,
     "description": "A limit reached its cap – halt the run"
    },
    {
     "name": "onStop",
     "type": "(state: BudgetGuardState) => void",
     "optional": true,
     "description": "\"Stop run\" / \"End run\" pressed"
    },
    {
     "name": "title",
     "type": "string",
     "optional": true,
     "description": "The heading, and the region's name"
    }
   ],
   "hides": [
    "limits",
    "heading"
   ],
   "events": {
    "tc-limits-change": "onRaise",
    "tc-cap-reach": "onCapReach",
    "tc-stop": "onStop"
   }
  }
 ],
 "changelog": [
  "`tc-budget-guard` – spend and token caps for a live run: a big meter and thin ones, the pace to the cap, a warning with Raise to buttons at `warnAt`, and a hard stop with an alert. `tc-limits-change` (cancelable), `tc-cap-reach` once per cap, `tc-stop`."
 ],
